From: SiliconLoop closed-loop development
Subject: [PATCH 0020] ai-agent: L2 respawn falls back to the builtin name

Incremental on 0017/0019 (tool_recover.c is new in 0017). L2 restart
spawned RUN_ELF_PATH (/data/ai_agent/bin/buggy_app), but buggy_app is a
NuttX builtin and nothing re-deploys an ELF there at boot (/data is
tmpfs and wipes on every reboot), so posix_spawn always failed and the
restart rung could never fire. Try the deployed path first, then fall
back to the builtin registration name so the same workload restarts
either way.

Verified 2026-11-04: scenario C rounds (bug mode: L1 ineffective ->
L2 restart -> fault re-manifests -> needs_human) see the respawned
task in ps and the ladder walks both rungs (see
docs/evidence/2026-11-04/).
--- a/src/tools/tool_recover.c
+++ b/src/tools/tool_recover.c
@@ -171,6 +171,8 @@
 {
     pid_t child;
     char *argv[3];
+    int rc;
+
     argv[0] = (char *)"buggy_app";
     if (mode && strcmp(mode, "normal") != 0) {
         argv[1] = (char *)mode;
@@ -178,7 +180,16 @@
     } else {
         argv[1] = NULL;
     }
-    return posix_spawn(&child, path, NULL, NULL, argv, NULL);
+    rc = posix_spawn(&child, path, NULL, NULL, argv, NULL);
+    if (rc != 0) {
+        /* SiliconLoop: RUN_ELF_PATH lives on /data (tmpfs, wiped on
+         * reboot) and nothing re-deploys it at boot, so the deployed
+         * ELF is often missing. Fall back to the builtin registration
+         * name so L2 restarts the same workload either way
+         * (M3 scenario C, 2026-11-04). */
+        rc = posix_spawn(&child, argv[0], NULL, NULL, argv, NULL);
+    }
+    return rc;
 }
 
 /* SiliconLoop: a stale PID file whose number was reused must never make
